gpui_apple: build the Metal library and pipelines once, off the main thread

The shader library and the eight render pipeline states depend only on the
device, but every `MetalRenderer::new` built them synchronously, on the main
thread, inside window creation. With `runtime_shaders` and an empty Metal
cache, `newLibraryWithSource` alone took ~810 ms of a cold first window
(hosted macos-15, debug, Time Profiler); the pipelines ~50 ms more.

Build them once per process for the first device on a background thread,
started by `prepare_pipelines` (or by the first renderer), and share them
between renderers. A renderer resolves them the first time a draw encodes a
batch; if the build is still running it waits on a condvar, so no frame is
drawn without them. A failed build still panics on that first draw with the
original message. Another device gets its own build. The background build
runs inside its own autorelease pool, popped on failure too.

